"vheap.kfx: the engine's heap, written over tier 1's (cells/heap.kfx,
 C332; docs/research/one-heap.md): one heap in Fixpt's format, its values
 Fixpt's (`value.rs`) and its objects Fixpt's bloblets and pairs (C318 to
 C330), its spaces, its allocation's state and its collector tier 1's.
 Here, the engine's kinds and immediates, its allocation (`alloc!`, from
 tier 1's `heap-top`, not zeroed: the engine writes every word of what it
 makes), its own objects' access (`obj-ref` in `alloc`'s order,
 `bloblet-value` in slots), and its roots given to tier 1's collector
 (`collect!`). Its two spaces are reserved whole and committed as they
 are touched, so that the heap grows by its limit, never by copying."

"Tags, immediates' kinds, objects' kinds."
(define imm-char i64 0)
(define imm-bool i64 1)
(define imm-unit i64 2)
(define imm-nil i64 3)
(define imm-prim i64 5)

"Objects' kinds, as an object's header says them: Fixpt's kind where the
 engine's object is Fixpt's (`layout.rs`'s `KINDS`; C318), else one past
 Fixpt's (200 on) until it is. A pair has no header: Fixpt's two words."
(define ob-pair i64 0)
(define ob-ref i64 10)
(define ob-sum i64 36)
(define ob-product i64 37)
"An FX-26 array and a bloblet (C215): Fixpt's plain bloblet (`%make-bloblet`,
 C326), its values in slots 0 on, a trailer always, its bytes its suffix."
(define ob-array i64 32)
(define ob-proc i64 8)
(define ob-cont i64 14)
(define ob-env i64 35)
(define ob-frame i64 202)
(define ob-ctor i64 203)
"`datum`'s vector (C77): its elements, words, as an array's."
(define ob-vector i64 3)
"A flat array (C220): Fixpt's (C327, vprims.kfx's `flat-made!`), its
 layout's code in its slot, its elements' bits its suffix."
(define ob-flatx i64 42)
"A table keyed by identity (C220): Fixpt's (C329, vprims.kfx's
 `eqtable-made!`), three fields and no trailer."
(define ob-eqtable i64 43)
"Kinds whose payload is raw words, not values: a bloblet's suffix, never
 traced, as Fixpt's. A string and a bytevector are Fixpt's (C320:
 words.kfx)."
(define ob-string i64 1)
"A symbol (C321): Fixpt's, its name (a string), its hash and its global
 slot, which in the engine holds its name's number (tier 1's holds 0: to
 settle once the heap is one); and a keyword, Fixpt's, its symbol."
(define ob-symbol i64 2)
(define ob-keyword i64 48)
(define ob-bytes i64 4)
(define ob-real i64 5)
(define ob-big i64 6)
(define raw-kind? (subr kfx (i64) bool)
  (lambda (k) (or (i64= k ob-string) (i64= k ob-bytes) (i64= k ob-real) (i64= k ob-big))))

"Making and taking apart words: Fixpt's tags (`value.rs`)."
(define fixnum-max i64 1152921504606846975)
(define fixnum-min i64 -1152921504606846976)
(define fixnum? (subr kfx (i64) bool) (lambda (w) (i64= (i64-and w 7) 0)))
(define fits-fixnum? (subr kfx (i64) bool) (lambda (n) (and (i64<= n fixnum-max) (i64>= n fixnum-min))))
(define fixnum (subr kfx (i64) i64) (lambda (n) (i64-shl n 3)))
(define fixnum-value (subr kfx (i64) i64) (lambda (w) (i64-shr w 3)))
"A pair (tag 001) or a bloblet (tag 100): an object, at its index from
 tier 1's `vbase` (cells/heap.kfx's `address`, `heap-ref`; C332), a
 pair's car, a bloblet's suffix's first word. A suffix ref (C326) is tier
 1's too (`is-sref?`, `make-sref`, `sref-owner`, `sref-offset`)."
(define pointer? (subr kfx (i64) bool) (lambda (w) (or (i64= (i64-and w 7) 4) (i64= (i64-and w 7) 1))))
(define bloblet-at (subr cread (i64) i64) (lambda (p) (heap-ref p t-bloblet)))
(define pair-at (subr cread (i64) i64) (lambda (i) (heap-ref i t-pair)))
(define suffix-ref (subr cread (i64 i64) i64) (lambda (owner at) (make-sref (address owner) at)))
(define immediate? (subr kfx (i64) bool) (lambda (w) (i64= (i64-and w 7) 3)))

"Fixpt's immediates' subtags, and the engine's own until they are objects."
(define sub-false i64 0)
(define sub-true i64 1)
(define sub-null i64 2)
(define sub-unit i64 3)
(define sub-unbound i64 7)
"A primitive, the engine's own immediate, past Fixpt's subtags: a
 procedure, which reaches compiled code through an adapter, as the
 engine's closures will (docs/research/one-heap.md, step 4)."
(define sub-prim i64 25)

(define imm-word (subr kfx (i64 i64) i64)
  (lambda (sub n) (i64+ (i64-shl n 8) (i64+ (i64-shl sub 3) 3))))
(define immediate-sub (subr kfx (i64) i64) (lambda (w) (i64-and (i64-shr w 3) 31)))

(define immediate (subr kfx (i64 i64) i64)
  (lambda (kind n)
    "The engine's immediate of `kind` (`imm-char` and the rest) and payload
     `n`, as Fixpt's subtag says it."
    (cond ((i64= kind imm-char) (imm-word sub-char n))
          ((i64= kind imm-bool) (imm-word (if (i64= n 0) sub-false sub-true) 0))
          ((i64= kind imm-unit) (imm-word sub-unit 0))
          ((i64= kind imm-nil) (imm-word sub-null 0))
          (else (imm-word sub-prim n)))))
(define immediate-kind (subr kfx (i64) i64)
  (lambda (w)
    (let ((sub (immediate-sub w)))
      (cond ((or (i64= sub sub-false) (i64= sub sub-true)) imm-bool)
            ((i64= sub sub-unit) imm-unit)
            ((i64= sub sub-null) imm-nil)
            ((i64= sub sub-char) imm-char)
            ((i64= sub sub-prim) imm-prim)
            (else -1)))))
(define immediate-value (subr kfx (i64) i64) (lambda (w) (i64-shr w 8)))
(define code-word (subr kfx (i64) i64) (lambda (i) (fixnum i)))
(define code-index (subr kfx (i64) i64) (lambda (w) (fixnum-value w)))

"Fixpt's constants (`value.rs`): `#f` 3, `#t` 11, `nil` 19, `#u` 27, the
 unbound marker 59."
(define w-unit i64 27)
(define w-nil i64 19)
(define w-true i64 11)
(define w-false i64 3)
(define w-unbound i64 59)

"The heap: tier 1's (cells/heap.kfx, C332): its spaces `mem` and `other`,
 its next free index `heap-top`, its `limit`, its collector and its count
 of collections."
"Each name's symbol and keyword, by its number, once made (0 until then):
 roots, so that each name has one object (C321)."
(define symbol-objects (ref (flatarrayof i64 @c) @c) (new (make-flatarray-i64 64 0)))
(define keyword-objects (ref (flatarrayof i64 @c) @c) (new (make-flatarray-i64 64 0)))

(define heap-start! (subr calloc (i64) unit)
  (lambda (words)
    "Tier 1's two spaces, each reserved at its capacity and committed as it
     is touched (C139), the first `words` words used at first (its
     `limit`); indices 0 to 7 never an object's."
    (begin
      (set mem (make-flatarray-i64 heap-capacity 0))
      (set other (make-flatarray-i64 heap-capacity 0))
      (set heap-top 8)
      (set limit words))))

(define heap-room (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @c)) () i64)
  (lambda ()
    "The room left, as the machine counts what a step needs: a header and a
     payload an object (C64). Two thirds of the words free, since Fixpt's
     layout (C318) gives an object of fields a trailer too, at most half as
     much again (one of a field); one of none has no trailer, and a pair is
     two words, not three."
    (i64-quotient (i64* (i64- (get limit) (get heap-top)) 2) 3)))

"Fixpt's headers (`layout.fx`): tag 110, the kind in bits 3 to 11, a
 large header's mark at bit 11, the fields (F, with the trailer) in bits
 14 to 32, the suffix's bytes (B) in bits 32 to 64; a large header's F
 in the extension word before it, kind 255, its F above bit 11. A
 trailer, the last field, is tag 101 and F above."
(define fields-max i64 262143)
(define header (subr kfx (i64 i64 i64) i64)
  (lambda (kind f b) (i64+ (i64-shl b 32) (i64+ (i64-shl f 14) (i64+ (i64-shl kind 3) 6)))))
(define large-header (subr kfx (i64 i64) i64)
  (lambda (kind b) (i64+ (i64-shl b 32) (i64+ 2048 (i64+ (i64-shl kind 3) 6)))))
(define extension (subr kfx (i64) i64) (lambda (f) (i64+ (i64-shl f 11) (i64+ (i64-shl 255 3) 6))))
(define trailer (subr kfx (i64) i64) (lambda (f) (i64+ (i64-shl f 3) 5)))
(define header-kind (subr kfx (i64) i64) (lambda (h) (i64-and (i64-shr h 3) 255)))
(define header-large? (subr kfx (i64) bool) (lambda (h) (i64= (i64-and (i64-shr h 11) 1) 1)))
(define header-fields (subr kfx (i64) i64) (lambda (h) (i64-and (i64-shr h 14) fields-max)))
(define header-bytes (subr kfx (i64) i64) (lambda (h) (i64-and (i64-shr h 32) 4294967295)))
(define extension-fields (subr kfx (i64) i64) (lambda (x) (i64-shr x 11)))
(define suffix-words (subr kfx (i64) i64) (lambda (b) (i64-quotient (i64+ b 7) 8)))

"A bloblet's main header's index, as tier 1's `header-index` finds it
 (`header-below`), the word below the suffix read by `at-word`."
(define header-at (subr cread (i64) i64)
  (lambda (v) (let ((p (address v))) (header-below p (mem-at (i64- p 1))))))

(define bump! (subr cwrite (i64) i64)
  (lambda (n)
    "`n` words of tier 1's heap, not zeroed, as `heap-alloc!` zeroes them:
     the engine writes each of an object it makes. The room was made sure
     of before the step."
    (let ((at (get heap-top)))
      (if (i64> (i64+ at n) (get limit))
          (begin (error "the engine's heap: a step allocated past the room it was given") 0)
          (begin (set heap-top (i64+ at n)) at)))))

(define alloc! (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @c) (write @c)) (i64 i64) i64)
  (lambda (kind n)
    "An object of `kind`, `n` words of payload, in Fixpt's layout (C318): a
     pair two words; an object of raw words a bloblet whose suffix they are;
     any other a bloblet of `n` fields and a trailer, so that payload word
     `i` is the word `i` after the header, as `alloc` lays it out. The room
     was made sure of before the step (`heap-ensure!`)."
    (cond ((i64= kind ob-pair) (pair-at (bump! 2)))
          ;; No fields: no trailer, the word below the suffix its header.
          ((or (raw-kind? kind) (i64= n 0))
           (let ((at (bump! (i64+ n 1)))) (begin (mem-set! at (header kind 0 (i64* 8 n))) (bloblet-at (i64+ at 1)))))
          (else
           (let ((f (i64+ n 1)))
             (if (i64> f fields-max)
                 (let ((at (bump! (i64+ f 2))))
                   (begin (mem-set! at (extension f)) (mem-set! (i64+ at 1) (large-header kind 0))
                          (mem-set! (i64+ at (i64+ f 1)) (trailer f))
                          (bloblet-at (i64+ at (i64+ f 2)))))
                 (let ((at (bump! (i64+ f 1))))
                   (begin (mem-set! at (header kind f 0)) (mem-set! (i64+ at f) (trailer f))
                          (bloblet-at (i64+ at (i64+ f 1)))))))))))

(define-rec
  (words-zeroed! (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @c) (write @c)) (i64 i64) unit)
    (lambda (i n) (if (i64<= n 0) #u (begin (mem-set! i 0) (words-zeroed! (i64+ i 1) (i64- n 1)))))))

(define bloblet-alloc! (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @c) (write @c)) (i64 i64) i64)
  (lambda (n bytes)
    "A plain bloblet (`make_bloblet`, C326): `n` fields and a trailer, the
     fields for the caller to fill, and a suffix of `bytes` bytes, all 0."
    (let* ((f (i64+ n 1)) (sw (suffix-words bytes)) (large (i64> f fields-max)) (at (bump! (i64+ (i64+ f sw) (if large 2 1))))
           (main (if large (i64+ at 1) at)))
      (begin (if large (begin (mem-set! at (extension f)) (mem-set! main (large-header ob-array bytes))) (mem-set! main (header ob-array f bytes)))
             (mem-set! (i64+ main f) (trailer f))
             (words-zeroed! (i64+ main (i64+ f 1)) sw)
             (bloblet-at (i64+ main (i64+ f 1)))))))

(define fields-alloc! (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @c) (write @c)) (i64 i64) i64)
  (lambda (kind n)
    "A bloblet of `n` fields and no trailer, nor suffix (`make_bloblet`'s,
     `trailer` false: an eqtable, C329): field `k`, from 1, at `p - k`
     (tier 1's `slot-of`), its header below them."
    (let ((at (bump! (i64+ n 1)))) (begin (mem-set! at (header kind n 0)) (bloblet-at (i64+ at (i64+ n 1)))))))

"An object's payload: a pair's two words; a bloblet's fields, found by its
 trailer (`p - F + i`), or, with none, its suffix (`p + i`)."
(define payload-at (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @c)) (i64 i64) i64)
  (lambda (v i)
    (if (is-pair? v)
        (i64+ (address v) i)
        (let* ((p (address v)) (b (mem-at (i64- p 1))))
          (if (i64= (word-tag b) 5) (i64+ (i64- p (i64-shr b 3)) i) (i64+ p i))))))

(define obj-kind (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @c)) (i64) i64)
  (lambda (v) (if (is-pair? v) ob-pair (header-kind (mem-at (header-at v))))))

(define obj-size (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @c)) (i64) i64)
  (lambda (v)
    (if (is-pair? v)
        2
        (let* ((p (address v)) (b (mem-at (i64- p 1))))
          (if (i64= (word-tag b) 5) (i64- (i64-shr b 3) 1) (i64-quotient (header-bytes b) 8))))))

(define obj-ref (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @c)) (i64 i64) i64)
  (lambda (v i) (mem-at (payload-at v i))))

(define obj-set! (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @c) (write @c)) (i64 i64 i64) unit)
  (lambda (v i w) (mem-set! (payload-at v i) w)))

"The engine's own objects, which only it reads (frames, environments,
 closures, continuations): payload word `i` is field `i + 2`, at `p - 2 -
 i`, Fixpt's `slot` order (`bloblet_slot`), no trailer read to find it
 (C318). Every other object's is `alloc`'s order, which Fixpt's code reads
 (`obj-ref`), its trailer read for its count of fields."
(define bloblet-value (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @c)) (i64 i64) i64)
  (lambda (v i) (mem-at (i64- (i64- (address v) 2) i))))
(define bloblet-value-set! (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @c) (write @c)) (i64 i64 i64) unit)
  (lambda (v i w) (mem-set! (i64- (i64- (address v) 2) i) w)))

"The collector: Cheney's, over Fixpt's objects. Each root copied, then
 the copies scanned, header by header (a word no header begins a pair);
 a moved object's forwarding, tag 111, its copy's index, in a pair's first
 word and in the word below a bloblet's suffix."

"The collector: tier 1's (C332), Coopt's baseline, given the engine's
 roots (`roots`, the globals, the constants, the names' symbols and
 keywords) between its start and its end, each forwarded in place; then
 room for what the step needs, as `heap-room` counts it, the limit
 raised if need be (`room!`)."
(define-rec
  (roots-forwarded! (subr calloc ((flatarrayof i64 @c) i64 i64) unit)
    (lambda (rs i n)
      (if (i64>= i n)
          #u
          (begin (flatarray-set-i64! rs i (forward! (flatarray-ref-i64 rs i))) (roots-forwarded! rs (i64+ i 1) n))))))

(define collect! (subr calloc ((flatarrayof i64 @c) (flatarrayof i64 @c) (flatarrayof i64 @c) i64) unit)
  (lambda (roots globals consts need)
    (begin
      (collect-begin!)
      (roots-forwarded! roots 0 (flatarray-length-i64 roots))
      (roots-forwarded! globals 0 (flatarray-length-i64 globals))
      (roots-forwarded! consts 0 (flatarray-length-i64 consts))
      (roots-forwarded! (get symbol-objects) 0 (flatarray-length-i64 (get symbol-objects)))
      (roots-forwarded! (get keyword-objects) 0 (flatarray-length-i64 (get keyword-objects)))
      (collect-end!)
      (room! (i64+ need (i64-quotient need 2))))))

"Interned names: symbols, tags, labels and label lists, each a number in a
 table of strings, made once a name, never freed."
(define names (ref (arrayof string @c) @c) (new (make-array 64 "")))
(define name-count (ref i64 @c) (new 0))

(define-rec
  (name-at (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @c)) (string i64 i64) i64)
    (lambda (s i n)
      (cond ((i64>= i n) -1)
            ((string=? (array-ref (get names) (i64->int i)) s) i)
            (else (name-at s (i64+ i 1) n))))))

(define-rec
  (names-copied! (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @c) (write @c)) ((arrayof string @c) (arrayof string @c) i64 i64) unit)
    (lambda (from to i n)
      (if (i64>= i n) #u (begin (array-set! to (i64->int i) (array-ref from (i64->int i))) (names-copied! from to (i64+ i 1) n))))))

(define intern! (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @c) (write @c) (alloc @c)) (string) i64)
  (lambda (s)
    "The number of name `s`, made if it has none."
    (let ((found (name-at s 0 (get name-count))))
      (if (i64>= found 0)
          found
          (let ((n (get name-count)))
            (begin
              (if (i64>= n (int->i64 (array-length (get names))))
                  (let ((bigger (the (arrayof string @c) (make-array (i64->int (i64* n 2)) ""))))
                    (begin (names-copied! (get names) bigger 0 n) (set names bigger)))
                  #u)
              (array-set! (get names) (i64->int n) s)
              (set name-count (i64+ n 1))
              n))))))

(define name-of-number (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @c)) (i64) string)
  (lambda (n) (array-ref (get names) (i64->int n))))
